      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "Most prokaryotes are unicellular. The nucleus is poorly defined due to the absence of a nuclear membrane. Nucleolus is absent. Cell organelles such as plastids, mitochondria, golgi bodies, etc. are absent. Bacteria and blue-green algae are prokaryotic cells. Most eukaryotes are multicellular. The nucleus is well defined and is surrounded by a nuclear membrane. Nucleolus is present. Cell organelles such as plastids, mitochondria, golgi bodies, etc. are present.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, eukaryotes have a well-defined nucleus and organelles, while prokaryotes do not.",
    "answer_image": {
